  "ruleNotes": "Each side occupies its nearest triangle (6 points) plus the two nearest rows of the square (10 points); the middle row of the square starts empty. Pieces move and capture in any direction along drawn lines; captures are by the short leap and are not mandatory, multiple captures are allowed but the player may stop, and capturing all opposing pieces wins.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "sources": [
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_soldiers (observed 2026-09-27): two triangular boards on opposite sides of a standard Alquerque board; each player occupies their half of the Alquerque board and nearest triangle; moves/captures in any direction along lines; Parker (Ancient Ceylon, 1909, p.583) rules: capture not mandatory, multiple captures allowed, capture-all wins",
    "https://skich.app/games/sholo-guti-16-bead-offline (observed 2026-09-27): 37 intersections, 16 pieces per side, middle line empty",
    "https://apkpure.net/bead-16-sholo-guti-sixteen-soldiers-board-game/com.yss.shologuti.bead16.damru.game.free (observed 2026-09-27): standard Alquerque plus two opposite triangles; middle line empty; starter agreed beforehand",
    "http://www.cyningstan.com/games/604/alquerque-games (observed 2026-09-27): standard Alquerque expanded with one triangle on each side, 16 pieces per player",
    "Physical Sholo Guti board product image, rollthedice.in (observed 2026-09-27): triangle extensions with 6 points each confirmed visually; triangle-to-square attachment at three points of the square edge",
